# Ask, do not invent

If anything is unknown, missing, incomplete, or uncertain — **stop and ask**. Do not guess. Do not fill gaps with invented values, assets, copy, API behavior, layout, or business rules.

Ask before continuing when:

- a design token, color, image, GIF, or dark/light variant is missing
- Figma, copy, or requirements do not specify a value or state
- UI behavior, edge cases, or API contracts are unclear
- you are not sure which existing component, screen, or pattern to reuse
- a previous decision in chat might be wrong or outdated

How to ask:

- say what is missing and why it blocks the work
- offer the smallest set of concrete options when that helps
- wait for an answer before writing or changing code

Do not:

- invent colors, spacing, copy, assets, or “close enough” stand-ins
- copy a background, image, or card color from another screen because it “looks similar”
- assume Dark/Light, iOS version, or device behavior without a source
- proceed with a guessed default and mention it only afterwards
- keep coding when Figma for **this** screen was not read in this turn
